        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e6ba0b050371451386688c43073b0e3b",
      "statement": "Card verification (verifyCard) is a two-step flow: first VERIFY_MERCHANT creates a transaction and returns a bank list plus transaction_id; then, depending on the bank, either card details are submitted (verifyCard) for ONEPAY banks or a SELECT_BANK request returns a bank redirect URL. Auth state is set to authorization_required with an approval link when the transaction proceeds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommGateway.java#L313-L355",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17017b8ef24b3f75dff272a658518ad5d7aa108b232f5d60f461e747e8220642:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommGateway.java#L47-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e3b72305ce26dad4f2eb6f20f82c83bb45e5602949ce75c1e5a26d3793caca29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7934c3e7bf7f46e5b7a8e26070ffda1b",
      "statement": "The gateway translates Onecomm response codes into internal states and reasons. A status of '1' indicates success; '2' indicates fraud (mapped to a FRAUD reason); non-success codes are mapped through property lookups (onecomm.status.<code>.code and .desc) with a default of ONECOMM_RESPONSE_CODE_NOT_MAP when unmapped. Refund responses map status 200 to FAILED, 300/100 to PENDING, and 400 to APPROVED.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommGateway.java#L1206-L1226",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e7554e2b326175fd5dd36f196ffd7b5d79fe46db47a9fabaf78d93700415e10:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/vn/onepay/pspconnector/provider/onecomm/OnecommPaymentServiceProvider.java#L463-L478",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a6da48dbc35ad1b22065397205388bd885078ecf1e98b4a64d10ee83b868f4d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b3d4a0f364104434bc6c5040c67242f1",
      "statement": "Gateway requests to the bank include vpc_* parameters (access code, amount, command, currency, merchant, transaction reference, return URL, etc.), signed with an HMAC-SHA256 hash computed over the alphabetically sorted vpc_/user_ prefixed fields using the merchant's secret hash code, appended as vpc_SecureHash.",
      "evidence": [
        {
